<article class="env-lemma" id="03TO">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03TO">Lemma <span data-tag="03TO">64.12.2</span>.</a> Let $\Lambda $ be a left Noetherian ring and $K\in D(\Lambda )$. Then $K$ is perfect if and only if the two following conditions hold: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$K$ has finite $\text{Tor}$-dimension, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for all $i \in \mathbf{Z}$, $H^ i(K)$ is a finite $\Lambda $-module. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      See More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0658" data-tag="0658">15.76.2</a> for the proof in the commutative case. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>